{%- comment -%}
mf2 u-syndication — the machine-readable link from a post to its copies
elsewhere.

Syndicating to Mastodon, Bluesky and LinkedIn is a core Indiekit feature
(each @rmdes/indiekit-syndicator-* plugin writes the resulting URL back into
the post), and u-syndication is the only way a consumer can tie a copy back
to its original. Without it Bridgy backfeed cannot associate a reply on
Mastodon with the post that produced it, so syndicated conversation never
comes home.

The source has no equivalent — it hardcodes single `tweet`/`toot` front
matter fields (post.liquid:16-20) rendered as visible prose links with no
mf2 class at all. This is the general form of that, so it is a deliberate
divergence rather than a port.

Rendered .sr-only: the data is fully available to parsers while the source's
visual design, which carries no syndication row, is preserved.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if syndication -%}
<ul class="sr-only">
{%- for syndicationUrl in syndication %}<li><a class="u-syndication" href="{{ syndicationUrl }}">{{ syndicationUrl }}</a></li>{% endfor -%}
</ul>
{%- endif -%}
